.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Boltzmann&#x27;s 1877 insight, written by Planck as S=k_B\ln W: entropy counts the microscopic arrangements W compatible with a macroscopic state. For N indistinguishable molecules on M lattice sites, W=\binom{M}{N}, and canonical_entropy evaluates k_B\ln W exactly via ln_binomial. The entropy is largest at half filling, where the number of arrangements peaks, and per site it converges to the Stirling-approximation mixing entropy -k_B[\theta\ln\theta+(1-\theta)\ln(1-\theta)] as M grows.">

